OA and OB are y=\frac{3}{4}x and y=\frac{1}{4}x, respectively.
Therefore, the triangle may be expressed as a vertically simple region by the following inequalities:
0\le x\le 4,\quad \frac{x}{4}\le y\le \frac{3x}{4}
The double integral of f( x,y )=24 y{e}^{x} over the triangle is the following iterated integral:
\begin{array}{rcl}
\int_0^4 \int_{x/4}^{3x/4} 24 y e^x \,dy \,dx \amp =\amp \int_0^4 \frac{24}{2} y^2 e^x\bigg|_{y=x/4}^{3x/4} \,dx\\ \amp =\amp \int_0^4 12 e^x\left(\frac{9 x^2}{16}-\frac{x^2}{16}\right)\,dx\\ \amp =\amp \int_0^4 \frac{12}{2} x^2 e^x \,dx \end{array} We use the integration formula \int {x}^2{e}^{x} \,dx={x}^2{e}^{x}-2x{e}^{x}+2{e}^{x}+C This gives
\begin{array}{rcl} \int_0^4 \int_{{x}/{4}}^{3x/4} 24 y e^x \,dy \,dx \amp =\amp \frac{12}{2}\int_0^4 x^2 e^x\,dx\\ \amp =\amp 6 x^2 e^x - 12 x e^x + 12 e^x \bigg|_0^4\\ \amp =\amp
6\cdot 16 e^4-12\cdot 4 e^4 + 12 e^4-12\\ \amp =\amp 60 e^4 -12 \approx 3263.89 \end{array}
